1. Process Model: Waterfall follows a strict sequential and linear model, whereas Agile follows an iterative and incremental development model.
2. Flexibility: Waterfall resists requirement changes after the planning phase, whereas Agile is highly flexible and welcomes changes at any time.
3. Delivery: Waterfall delivers the finished software only at the end of the project, whereas Agile delivers functional software pieces regularly at the end of every sprint.
